{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1293682-is-the-aura-system-easier-to-use-than-it-looks","id":1293682,"title":"Is the Aura system easier to use than it looks?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-03-04T01:53:01-08:00","id":1293682,"title":"Is the Aura system easier to use than it looks?","content":"Terrestrials' Elemental Aura system looks like it has a lot of moving parts and involves a lot of bookkeeping, tracking which Charms are and aren't keyworded, and which ones have which Aura. Is it as awkward and time-consuming as it looks? How much of a pain is the question of, &quot;This Charm is clearly advantageous, but using it would knock me out of my current Aura/put me into an Aura I don't want?&quot; I haven't had the opportunity to actually play, and don't expect to get the opportunity at any time in the foreseeable future, so I'm seeking enlightenment from those more fortunate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1856-hakkonen","name":"Hakkonen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T03:48:33-08:00","id":1293690,"title":"","content":"It really depends on what you're trying to do with it.<br /> Normally there's two main aura states to consider - your Aspect's (because you enter it automatically the round when you go totemic) and the one most of your main combat tree is (which might be the same as your Aspect or an element neutral Martial Art) though I should note that both games I'm drawing upon are relatively low xp and haven't had the PCs try to match moves with Celestial Exalts, which I think will be where moving to different auras might be more necessary to keep up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T03:57:46-08:00","id":1293692,"title":"","content":"We haven't been able to run much more than some quick tests with DBs yet.<br /> <br /> That said, play aids seem to have made a huge difference at the table. Tracking when your Aura state changes wasn't too bad, but trying to remember what it should be was a pain with just the text. Having six solid colored cards or a big die (one neutral, five for each Aura) to say &quot;this is what you're in now,&quot; and Charm cards color and symbol coded well so you could hold you Charms like a hand in cards and readily line up which were compatible and which weren't seemed to help significantly.<br /> <br /> We didn't see that much debating over 'stay in Aura or use this other useful Charm' in play, but that's mostly because Charm selection was on the slow side front-loading that. So most character's default combat platter was designed around one or two elements anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T05:52:32-08:00","id":1293715,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ll second play aides. I\u2019m planning on 3-d printing dice where 5 of the sides have the 5 elemental dragon mons engraved into them and splashed with a bit of enamel paint, and the sixth side being blank. That way everyone can keep track of their aura easier.<br /> <br /> I really like the charm card idea, it\u2019s almost like magic the gathering. <br /> <br /> <br /> From my meagre experiences the system isn\u2019t as bad as it looks because DBs don\u2019t have a whole lot of stuff that combos, and what does combo does so fairly intuitively. So like the earth aspect brawler with only earth aspect and balanced brawl charms didn\u2019t have to worry about it at all, but I imagine if he\u2019d picked up a purely water charm or a water aura charm he\u2019d be able to manage it pretty well. It might help to start off slow and get a really solid feel for what you have and then add on bits as you get more comfortable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T06:09:23-08:00","id":1293720,"title":"","content":"The pay aides sound cool, but also kind of damning for the keyword.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25050-fodor","name":"FODOR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T07:19:11-08:00","id":1293742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FODOR</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1293682-is-the-aura-system-easier-to-use-than-it-looks?p=1293720#post1293720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The pay aides sound cool, but also kind of damning for the keyword.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah possibly, for context though my group also uses a physical number line to track initiative and each of us have either an abacus or bead boxes for mote counting. I\u2019m not sure if it\u2019s super necessary but it\u2019s helpful for sure and kind of fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T07:34:59-08:00","id":1293745,"title":"","content":"Sure, context is a hell of a thing, and being a lazy soul I'm used to doing it all in my head with the occasional scribbling numbers down on the back of the character sheet so yet another thing to keep track of puts the willies up me. If you're used to using stuff already then adding one more bit of gubbins probably doesn't feel as extreme.<br /> <br /> Maybe I'll try using some physical props to help bookkeeping.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25050-fodor","name":"FODOR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T07:47:13-08:00","id":1293749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FODOR</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1293682-is-the-aura-system-easier-to-use-than-it-looks?p=1293745#post1293745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, context is a hell of a thing, and being a lazy soul I'm used to doing it all in my head with the occasional scribbling numbers down on the back of the character sheet so yet another thing to keep track of puts the willies up me. If you're used to using stuff already then adding one more bit of gubbins probably doesn't feel as extreme.<br /> <br /> Maybe I'll try using some physical props to help bookkeeping.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019d say it\u2019s almost transformative to the game. Like using big complex maps and terrain in DnD. Theatre of the mind is great sometimes bit that really transforms it into a tactics war game. Likewise if you can just trust that your tray of beads is accurate you can focus on the important stuff. Not to mention looking at a big pile of Essence 3 Solar motes in physical form can be a heady feeling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T08:08:10-08:00","id":1293753,"title":"","content":"There's two states to it. If you play a character who uses their Aspect's primary combat ability /Air Aspect with Thrown, Fire with Melee, etc) or uses their Aspect's Immaculate MA, then its the easiest thing in the universe.<br /> If you choose to play off element, like say a Water Aspect Melee fighter, it's hell.<br /> (I did the later because I'm obviously a masochist).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T08:27:06-08:00","id":1293762,"title":"","content":"That was my impression. Though even with all your own aura stuff, it's still going to take a turn before it activates.<br /> <br /> (Though a Water-Aspected fighter is really, really good... when you're in the right mode, which is really difficult.)<br /> <br /> I have a friend who runs a game of mostly DBs, Essence 3, and he said two players had the hang of it (or... maybe one has the hang of it, and the other just took all the same Aspect so it didn't matter?), and used quite powerful stuff, but everyone else avoided it as they found it intimidating, which meant they weren't using the most powerful effects.<br /> He said that a couple of sessions after converting to 3rd ed though, so I don't know if it's changed since then.<br /> <br /> I asked one of the players, he said &quot;Not great. Not terrible. Not a headache, but something you can forget to keep track of.&quot; Fodor plays with those players though, even if he's the only one not playing a DB, so he'd probably have a more accurate view.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T08:28:13-08:00","id":1293763,"title":"","content":"I'm a long-time fan of physical play aides, like charm cards and mote beads, for Exalted. Deep in its bones, I contend that Exalted is a card game in the same way that D&amp;D is a war game.<br /> <br /> TBH I think Exalted could do with embracing those elements even more, in the same vein as D&amp;D brought back miniatures-on-a-map in a big way starting around 3e. There's always been a weird tension in Exalted that I trace back to trying to be a Classic Era White Wolf game focused on story and characters and drama, AND a wonky, rules-heavy combat game at the same time. IMO that's kept many designers from fully embracing the potential of leaning into the physical elements of game design, because it's like admitting it's really a game and not just a narrative engine.<br /> <br /> Auras are a great example; the mechanics are cool and interesting but fiddly and complex to track; could we get an &quot;at the table&quot; sidebar somewhere explaining how the designer expects it to <i>work</i> in the context of human beings playing the game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","user":"Blackwell","date":". 03-04-2019, 11:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T08:32:29-08:00","id":1293766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FODOR</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1293682-is-the-aura-system-easier-to-use-than-it-looks?p=1293720#post1293720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The pay aides sound cool, but also kind of damning for the keyword.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why? Adding a widget to the system is never meant to make the system SIMPLER.<br /> <br /> Among other things, Aura is supposed to be a way to justify giving Dragon-Blooded the ability to punch outside of their weight-class while still keeping them in that lower weight-class.<br /> <br /> Aura doesn't exist to punish you by forcing you to jump through hoops. Aura exists to reward you for playing to Aspect stereotypes or successfully jumping through hoops.<br /> <br /> If you're a Fire Aspect who fights with Melee and only picks Balanced or Fire-aspected combat Charms from out-of-Aspect Abilities, Aura is a rare concern because you're almost always in Fire Aura.<br /> <br /> Especially if you avoid non-Fire Melee Charms like Flowing Graceful Defense, but you'll probably get that one to use in emergencies where losing your Fire Aura is an acceptable price.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T08:35:25-08:00","id":1293769,"title":"","content":"I play over Skype, so I have notepad or my character sheet (which is a .doc file) open and just write on there motes, initiative, etc, and then change it as it goes.<br /> <br /> Charm cards is kind of a good idea....<br /> But I have 40 charms. That's a bit much to be sorting through charm cards.<br /> I copy-paste the charm text onto my character sheet, edit them a bit for simplicity, write upgrade charms into the main text, change equations ([essence] dice, etc) to the appropriate number, and then organise them by situation (withering attacks, decisive attacks, defence, investigating stuff, social stuff).<br /> <br /> ... My Night Caste's character sheet was 14 pages long. At font size 8. Fine for a sheet on a computer, probably not for a physical sheet.<br /> Admittedly, he did have 400xp. It's probably easier at Essence 1.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T08:48:17-08:00","id":1293779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1293682-is-the-aura-system-easier-to-use-than-it-looks?p=1293766#post1293766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why? Adding a widget to the system is never meant to make the system SIMPLER.<br /> <br /> Among other things, Aura is supposed to be a way to justify giving Dragon-Blooded the ability to punch outside of their weight-class while still keeping them in that lower weight-class.<br /> <br /> Aura doesn't exist to punish you by forcing you to jump through hoops. Aura exists to reward you for playing to Aspect stereotypes or successfully jumping through hoops.<br /> <br /> If you're a Fire Aspect who fights with Melee and only picks Balanced or Fire-aspected combat Charms from out-of-Aspect Abilities, Aura is a rare concern because you're almost always in Fire Aura.<br /> <br /> Especially if you avoid non-Fire Melee Charms like Flowing Graceful Defense, but you'll probably get that one to use in emergencies where losing your Fire Aura is an acceptable price.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't expect it to make things simpler, but not every addition is the same as adding extra bookkeeping to a game already awfully heavy on it. Now maybe it's not so bad in actual play, I haven't had the opportunity, which is why I'm quite interested in the responses to this thread. In reading it Aura does feel very mechanistic and hoop-jumpy to me and not something that gives me an organic feeling of raw expressions of elemental power like I'd hope, which is a shame because a lot of the Aura effects are exactly what I'd like to see DB do<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25050-fodor","name":"FODOR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T09:19:29-08:00","id":1293789,"title":"","content":"I think maybe there's a difference between charms that become more powerful in Aura (like the Immaculate Martial Arts), and charms that actually require Aura to use at all.<br /> <br /> One you get benefits but you become more powerful in Aura, the other feels more like a hoop.<br /> <br /> Though the second ones are actually mechanically simpler.<br /> <br /> All-in-all I think it's a <i>balanced</i> system, it just looks awkward.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T09:24:34-08:00","id":1293793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FODOR</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1293682-is-the-aura-system-easier-to-use-than-it-looks?p=1293720#post1293720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The pay aides sound cool, but also kind of damning for the keyword.</div> </div> </div> </div>The question is what other things they keep a visual representation of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T09:37:10-08:00","id":1293798,"title":"","content":"I wonder if it would have been simpler if the Aura keyword was split in half; say split 'Need Aura to use' and 'Become more powerful in Aura', one stays Aura and the other becomes 'Empowered' instead. Though that leaves out 'Ones that let you expend Aura' I guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T09:55:27-08:00","id":1293809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1293682-is-the-aura-system-easier-to-use-than-it-looks?p=1293769#post1293769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Admittedly, he did have 400xp. It's probably easier at Essence 1.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like if the Exalted system was to be translated into sound, then at 400xp celestial exalted it would be the sound of a turbofan jet engine mere seconds before it\u2019s bearings exploded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T10:00:50-08:00","id":1293810,"title":"","content":"Yeah, somewhat.<br /> <br /> I mean, it's still decent. It's just really hard for players to remember how all their charms work.<br /> Though there's a big difference between having, say, 8 charms in 5 different areas, or 25 combat charms and 15 social charms. It's the combos that make it hard. For example, I have 6 or 7 medicine charms for my Lunar, and 3 craft charms, I don't need to know how to combine those with combat charms.<br /> <br /> I'm hoping to run a 0xp game once the Lunars KS is fully out. I'm really excited by a game where people only have 15 charms, all Essence 1, instead of 40-odd. I think they might be able to get the hang of all their charms. Especially if they take ox-bodies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T12:17:17-08:00","id":1293849,"title":"","content":"That\u2019s what I noticed from my DB tests. When you\u2019re a DB swordsman with just the excellency, crossfire slash, burning fury wreath and crimson fang bite, figuring out what to attack with is easy.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m really hoping that leads to combats that take the same time as solar ones, but end up being more rounds of dynamic fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T12:54:22-08:00","id":1293859,"title":"","content":"My group is currently playing dragon blooded and this hasn't been a issue. One person uses cards, another glass beads, and I just play to type and only pick charms for combat that involve only the wood or balanced keywords so it has never been a problem. Out of combat it isn't hard to keep track of at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2302-snakesandsuns","name":"Snakesandsuns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2302_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T19:45:25-08:00","id":1293943,"title":"","content":"In my 1-1 DB campaign, in which the player is a relatively mechanics-averse roleplayer, she finds the Aura system actually really fun to play around in. She has about 3 different Aura benefits she can get in combat (Earth-War, Fire-Melee/flurry social, Melee penalty negator; I think she also has a Air benefit she could technically pick up) but doesn't find them more oppressive than &quot;remembering to use Charms in the first place&quot;. She likes that unifying her techniques benefits her style, but that she can choose to go elsewhere for other neat abilities. It helps that, in general, Aura benefits for different Elements in the same trees do different things, so she's not needed to consider whether she should be in Fire or (?Wood) aura- it's fire for murdering and Wood for getting off her back foot and getting to a position of power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12692-whybover","name":"Whybover","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T06:58:30-08:00","id":1294028,"title":"","content":"Regarding play aides, for my Solar campaign we did use Charm cards and bead motes, as well as minis for positioning (with little plastic buckets for close) and an initiative tracker. It kept play moving. <br /> <br /> DrLoveMonkey, when you get that 3d die design complete, could you share it for others who might want to get them printed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T07:19:14-08:00","id":1294034,"title":"","content":"I'm having similar concern for running DB's as antagonists. We have a Wyld Hunt bearing down on the PC's and I'm in process of building serious contenders to stand against the Ccircle; buuuut, the Aura seems like a lot of moving parts for me to focus on. Will I make my antagonists too powerful by mostly just ignoring aura difficulties..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T07:22:57-08:00","id":1294037,"title":"","content":"I've only played a few sessions of DBs, and only online, but LCA handles aura and charms pretty well. Admittedly in the game we didn't have many times to worry about Aura, but hey.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T08:49:40-08:00","id":1294072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Janissary87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1293682-is-the-aura-system-easier-to-use-than-it-looks?p=1294034#post1294034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm having similar concern for running DB's as antagonists. We have a Wyld Hunt bearing down on the PC's and I'm in process of building serious contenders to stand against the Ccircle; buuuut, the Aura seems like a lot of moving parts for me to focus on. Will I make my antagonists too powerful by mostly just ignoring aura difficulties..</div> </div> </div> </div>For NPCs, I think it's not so bad; just build them so the Auras are easy. Either don't bother with Aura charms, or give them all the same elemental stuff so they go straight into Aura and stay there. Something like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T10:36:02-08:00","id":1294105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1293682-is-the-aura-system-easier-to-use-than-it-looks?p=1294072#post1294072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For NPCs, I think it's not so bad; just build them so the Auras are easy. Either don't bother with Aura charms, or give them all the same elemental stuff so they go straight into Aura and stay there. Something like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the other option I'm considering, but my impression of the Aura mechanics was that it squeezes flavor and potency into the DB; power that they'll definitely need when they go up against my players.<br /> <br /> X2 edged sword, yadde yadde yadda,","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T10:43:26-08:00","id":1294107,"title":"","content":"Sure, but you could go all in on one aura. You know, have an Earth Aspect with loads of Earth Aura charms, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T11:38:19-08:00","id":1294115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tikor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1293682-is-the-aura-system-easier-to-use-than-it-looks?p=1294028#post1294028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding play aides, for my Solar campaign we did use Charm cards and bead motes, as well as minis for positioning (with little plastic buckets for close) and an initiative tracker. It kept play moving. <br /> <br /> DrLoveMonkey, when you get that 3d die design complete, could you share it for others who might want to get them printed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure! Although I wouldn't hold your breath about it, I'm a mechanical engineer, not an artist, so my 3-d design skills are somewhat different than what's required for this. I could end up getting several hours into it and realize I'm not making any progress. Worst case scenario you could always print out little pictures, cut and glue the, to a die and then coat it in a clear hard resin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T11:45:03-08:00","id":1294119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Janissary87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1293682-is-the-aura-system-easier-to-use-than-it-looks?p=1294105#post1294105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's the other option I'm considering, but my impression of the Aura mechanics was that it squeezes flavor and potency into the DB; power that they'll definitely need when they go up against my players.<br /> <br /> X2 edged sword, yadde yadde yadda,</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're running a really complex fight against very powerful players you could just assume the DBs are in aura at all times and not worry about it. They make certain effects more powerful, but not overwhelmingly so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T14:23:10-08:00","id":1294175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Janissary87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1293682-is-the-aura-system-easier-to-use-than-it-looks?p=1294034#post1294034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will I make my antagonists too powerful by mostly just ignoring aura difficulties.</div> </div> </div> </div> Assuming the PCs are Solars, there is no such thing as <i>too powerful</i>, particularly not when you're bringing the Wyld Hunt to bear.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}